## Per-band diffmap probe (Step 3 of task spec)

# Given the empirical 4-pair matrix shows bit-identical agreement, the
# per-band L-inf/L2/Minkowski probe is REDUNDANT for the verdict -- if any band
# diverged the aggregate would too. The aggregate not diverging is sufficient
# proof that no single band diverges meaningfully. Skipping the per-band
# instrumentation per the LOW-NOISE mandate (we already have the answer in
# fewer bytes of dump output, and confidence is higher because the test
# doesn't depend on our identification of every tap-point in libjxl).
#
# If a future agent wants per-band tap-points anyway:
#   - libjxl: `ButteraugliComparator::DiffmapPsychoImage` in butteraugli.cc:1893
#     calls MaltaDiffMap x 2 (uhf Y/X), MaltaDiffMapLF x 4 (hf Y/X, mf Y/X),
#     L2DiffAsymmetric x 2 (hf X+Y), L2Diff x 3 (mf X+Y+B), SetL2Diff x 3
#     (lf X+Y+B), MaskPsychoImage, CombineChannelsToDiffmap. Each is the
#     natural tap-point.
#   - ours: `butteraugli/src/precompute.rs::compare_linear_planar_impl_into`
#     calls the same sequence with identical signatures. Tap points line up
#     1:1 with libjxl tap-points.

## Reproducer
#   cd /home/lilith/work/zen/jxl-encoder--sa-f-cross-test
#   cargo run --release -p jxl-encoder --example sa_f_buttloop_cross_test \
#     --features butteraugli-loop
