## Follow-on candidate: W44-AUDIT-9 (NOT in SA-F scope)

# Investigate AC strategy SEARCH partial-picks on smooth photo at e9 d=4.
# SA-A (commit 5c99dc20) finding: clic_22ea12 has 576 blocks with non-DCT8x8
# AC strategies in OUR encoder vs ZERO in cjxl. These different transforms
# produce a different recon, and the recon scores worse (4.14 -> 3.87 means
# our recon scores 7% BETTER on butteraugli than cjxl's recon on butteraugli).
#
# Two angles:
#   (a) Our encoder's AC-strategy SEARCH is too aggressive on smooth content
#       at high effort (libjxl bails out earlier for smooth content); OR
#   (b) Our recon at 3.87 is actually BETTER than cjxl's 4.14 (we save 1.2 KB
#       AND score better) -- in which case this is a WIN not a wedge.
# The asymmetry (we're smaller AND score better) suggests (b) more strongly,
# but SA-B's 2.4x iter-0 ratio cited as evidence of bad recon was due to
# DIFFERENT iter-0 intermediate state, not the final encode quality.
#
# Recommend opening W44-AUDIT-9 with a wider sweep (10-20 cells around the
# smooth-photo wedge band) measuring FINAL recon scores and bytes to
# determine whether (b) holds at scale, before fixing what may not be broken.
